What is the TCP/IP Model?
The TCP/IP Model is a set of rules that allows computers to communicate over a network.
Think of it as the language of the Internet.
If two computers follow these rules, they can exchange data without any problem.

Why Do We Need TCP/IP?

Imagine everyone spoke a different language.

One person speaks English.
Another speaks Kannada.
Another speaks Japanese.

Communication would be difficult.

Similarly, computers also need common rules.

TCP/IP provides those rules so every device connected to the Internet can communicate.
